From e6021387c81328ddb312651237c88123cef961e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Blichmann <cblichmann@google.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:22:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Integrate KML

Port Kernel Mode Linux (KML) to Linux 7.3 for x86_64, AArch64, and ARM:

- Add CONFIG_KERNEL_MODE_LINUX and CONFIG_KML_CHECK_CHROOT Kconfig options
  and Sphinx documentation under Documentation/admin-guide/kml.rst.
- Launch trusted ELF binaries under /trusted/ in kernel privilege mode via
  start_kernel_thread() in fs/binfmt_elf.c, with chroot safety checks.
- Authorize kernel-address uaccess for TIF_KU tasks (replacing the legacy
  set_fs(KERNEL_DS) mechanism removed in Linux 5.10-5.19).
- Implement x86_64 Ring-0 user execution using a dedicated __KML_CS GDT
  descriptor, per-CPU IST_INDEX_KML interrupt/exception stack switching,
  signal/syscall CS/SS preservation, and SMEP/SMAP disablement.
- Implement 64-bit ARM (AArch64) EL1t (SPSel=0, PSR_MODE_EL1t) execution,
  routing EL1t vectors through kernel_entry 0, 64 / ret_to_user, clearing
  PTE_PXN and user-table *_TABLE_PXN bits for executable user VMAs,
  recording EL1t status in TPIDRRO_EL0, disabling PAN/S1PIE/kernel-PAC
  conflicts, and preserving EL1t PSTATE across fork/clone, ptrace, and
  signal delivery.
- Port 32-bit ARM SYSTEM_MODE execution, exception vector dispatch, and
  TIF_KU handling to Linux 7.3.
