index 000000000..c3a462f35
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/admin-guide/kml.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+.. SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+
+=================
+Kernel Mode Linux
+=================
+
+Kernel Mode Linux (http://web.yl.is.s.u-tokyo.ac.jp/~tosh/kml)
+Copyright 2004, 2005 Toshiyuki Maeda
+
+Introduction
+============
+
+Kernel Mode Linux (KML) is a mechanism that executes selected user-space
+programs at the processor's kernel privilege level. Under Kernel Mode Linux,
+trusted user programs execute as ordinary user processes (with normal virtual
+memory, paging, signals, and scheduling), except that they run with kernel-mode
+CPU privilege and can access kernel address space and invoke kernel functions
+directly without costly hardware privilege-level transitions.
+
+Supported Architectures
+=======================
+
+- ``x86_64`` (Ring 0 via dedicated ``__KML_CS`` 64-bit code segment and IST
+  exception/interrupt stack switching, with ``PREEMPT_RT`` support)
+- ``arm64`` (AArch64 ``EL1t`` / ``PSR_MODE_EL1t`` with ``SPSel = 0``, user
+  executable page-table ``PXN`` cleared, and ``PREEMPT_RT`` support)
+- ``arm`` (32-bit ARM ``SYSTEM_MODE`` when CPU domains and PAN are disabled)
+
+Usage
+=====
+
+1. Enable ``CONFIG_KERNEL_MODE_LINUX=y`` (and optionally
+   ``CONFIG_KML_CHECK_CHROOT=y``) in the kernel configuration.
+   On ``x86_64``, ensure ``CONFIG_MITIGATION_PAGE_TABLE_ISOLATION=n`` and
+   ``CONFIG_X86_FRED=n``. On ``arm64``, ensure ``CONFIG_UNMAP_KERNEL_AT_EL0=n``,
+   ``CONFIG_ARM64_PAN=n``, ``CONFIG_ARM64_SW_TTBR0_PAN=n``, and
+   ``CONFIG_ARM64_PIE=n``. On ``arm``, ensure ``CONFIG_ARM_PAN=n``.
+2. Build and boot the kernel.
+3. Place trusted ELF executables in the ``/trusted/`` directory on the root
+   filesystem and invoke them via ``/trusted/<program>``:
+
+   .. code-block:: sh
+
+      # mkdir -p /trusted
+      # cp my_rt_task /trusted/
+      # /trusted/my_rt_task
+
+   Any ELF binary outside ``/trusted/`` (or inside a ``chroot`` environment when
+   ``CONFIG_KML_CHECK_CHROOT=y``) continues to execute in standard unprivileged
+   user mode.
+
+Implementation Notes
+====================
+
+- **x86_64**: ``load_elf_binary()`` invokes ``start_kernel_thread()`` for
+  trusted binaries under ``/trusted/``, setting ``CS = __KML_CS`` (CPL 0),
+  ``SS = __KERNEL_DS``, and the ``TIF_KU`` thread flag. Hardware interrupts and
+  exceptions use a dedicated IST stack (``IST_INDEX_KML``) so user stacks are
+  never written by the CPU prior to stack switching, and SMEP/SMAP are cleared
+  at boot when KML is enabled.
+- **arm64**: ``start_kernel_thread()`` initializes ``PSTATE`` to
+  ``PSR_MODE_EL1t`` (``SPSel = 0``, so user execution uses ``SP_EL0`` while
+  exceptions automatically switch to the task kernel stack in ``SP_EL1``), sets
+  ``TIF_KU`` and ``TPIDRRO_EL0 = 1``, clears ``PTE_PXN`` and hierarchical
+  user-table ``PXNTable`` bits on executable user mappings, and routes ``EL1t``
+  vectors through ``kernel_entry 0, 64`` / ``ret_to_user``.
+- **ARM**: ``start_kernel_thread()`` initializes ``CPSR`` to ``SYSTEM_MODE``
+  (``0x1f``) and sets ``TIF_KU``, while the exception vector stubs route mode
+  ``0xf`` entries to the user-mode handlers.
