+	  before executing user processes in kernel mode. In the current KML
+	  implementation, programs in the directory "/trusted" are executed in
+	  kernel mode. Therefore, the chroot check ensures that if the root file
+	  system is chrooted to "/home/foo/", programs in "/home/foo/trusted"
+	  are not accidentally executed in kernel mode.
+
+	  If you don't know what to do here, say Y.
